    "why": "The tour now tests the theology emotionally through Jonah. Jonah throws God’s covenant name back at him—“abounding in steadfast love”—because he cannot accept mercy shown to enemies. The discussion’s comparison with the laborers paid equally exposes a genuinely different reading pressure: mercy can look unjust from the viewpoint of those who believe they have earned God’s favor. This keeps the passage from becoming a comfortable list of attributes and shows why its mercy is morally disruptive.",
